    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nTelephone numbers are now stored, returned, and compared in **E.164 form**. The core logic lives in `TelephoneNormalizer`, which both request-normalization and duplicate-detection share.\n\n**Conversion rule (`toE164`):**\n- If the raw value starts with `+`, keep the country code \u2014 strip every non-digit and re-prefix `+` (e.g. `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456`).\n- Otherwise assume country code `+61`, drop a single leading `0` from the national digits, and prefix `+61` (e.g. `0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`).\n- Spaces, dashes, brackets \u2014 any non-digit \u2014 are stripped.\n- `normalize()` rejects with `InvalidTelephoneException` (\u2192 400) unless there are 8\u201315 digits after the `+`; `canonicalize()` applies the same transform without rejecting, for comparing existing owners.\n\n**Files changed:**\n1. `rest/validation/TelephoneNormalizer.java` \u2014 replaced the 10-digit logic with E.164 conversion + the 8\u201315 digit bound; shared `toE164` helper.\n2. `model/Owner.java` \u2014 telephone `@Pattern` is now `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$` (E.164); removed the obsolete `@Digits(integer=10)` and its import. This is what turned the first run's `500 ConstraintViolationException` into passing creates.\n3. `rest/advice/InvalidTelephoneException.java` & `ExceptionControllerAdvice.java` \u2014 javadoc updated to describe the E.164 rule.\n4. `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 telephone field description and example updated (regenerates the DTOs).\n\n**Duplicate detection** now compares E.164 values: the new owner's normalized number against each existing owner's `canonicalize`d telephone. Seed data (10-digit, e.g. `6085551023`) is loaded via SQL, bypassing bean validation, and canonicalizes to `+616085551023` for comparison \u2014 no collision with the AU test numbers.\n\nTest suite: **3/3 pass, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the three new acceptance checks (`coreNationalToE164`, `functionalityKeepsExplicitCountryCode`, `errorRejectsUnformattable`).",
